==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[use to]], [[usta]] {{a|colloquial}}

===Pronunciation===
* yo͞ost to͞o, {{IPAchar|/juːst.tu/}}, /<tt>ju:st tu<tt>/<!--note: the final "u" deliberately has no ː/: symbol after it in IPA and SAMPA-->
* {{audio|en-us-used_to.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{term|used||lang=en}}, past participle of {{term|use#Verb|use|lang=en|to perform habitually}} + {{term|to#Preposition|to}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|pos=[[used]] [[to#Preposition|to]]}}

# {{idiom|with noun phrase}} [[accustomed]] to, tolerant or accepting of.
#: ''I am '''used to''' cleaning up other people’s mess.''
#: ''I became '''used to''' his ways.''

